1
00:07:21,428 --> 00:07:27,428
One man alone understood the savagery of the
early American west from both sides.

2
00:14:42,857 --> 00:14:48,857
Ulzana's Raid is a western film directed by Robert Aldrich.

3
00:22:04,285 --> 00:22:10,285
After fierce war chief Ulzana and a small war party jump the reservation bent on murder and
terror, an inexperienced young lieutenant is assigned to track him down.

4
00:29:25,714 --> 00:29:31,714
McIntosh, played by Burt Lancaster.

5
00:36:47,142 --> 00:36:53,142
Lt. Garnett DeBuin, played by Bruce Davison.

6
00:44:08,571 --> 00:44:14,571
Ke-Ni-Tay, played by Jorge Luke.

7
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Sergeant, played by Richard Jaeckel.

8
00:58:51,428 --> 00:58:57,428
Ulzana, played by Joaquín Martínez.

9
01:06:12,857 --> 01:06:18,857
Captain Gates, played by Lloyd Bochner.

10
01:13:34,285 --> 01:13:40,285
Ulzana's Raid is a 1972 American revisionist Western film starring Burt
Lancaster, Richard Jaeckel, Bruce Davison, and Joaquin Martinez.

11
01:20:55,714 --> 01:21:01,714
Filmed on location in Arizona, it was directed by Robert
Aldrich based on a script by Alan Sharp.

12
01:28:17,142 --> 01:28:23,142
It portrays a brutal raid by Chiricahua Apaches
against American settlers in 1880s Arizona.

13
01:35:38,571 --> 01:35:44,571
The film explores themes of ambush, indian territory,
apache nation, lieutenant, rape victim.
